  "body": {
    "focus": "Stamp ledger records with their work item's label, anchor and kind\n\nRoot cause: the CR, BUILD and TESTS writers resolve the work item's folder identity (createdAtISO, workItemKind, epicSlug) only to place the md (codeReviewArtifactPaths / buildArtifactPaths / testsArtifactPaths) and never store it in the record's meta, so deriveMdPath on the stored meta resolves a different folder.\n\nFix intent: when a CR, BUILD or TESTS record is written, store in its meta the label, anchor and work-item kind the writer already resolved to place its markdown (epicSlug when the work item has a real label, epicCreatedAt, and standalone: true for a standalone item), so stored meta and md location agree. Only new writes change; no other meta or body fields.",
    "producesLld": false,
    "commit": "47761e49",
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "passed": true
      }
    ],
    "summary": "The BUILD, TESTS and code-review writers now store the epicSlug, epicCreatedAt and standalone flag they resolved to place the record's md (new folderIdentityMeta helper in storage.ts), so a path derived from the record's own meta is the md it was written to. Regression tests in src/workflow/__tests__/ledger-record-identity.test.ts fail without the fix and pass with it.",
